summary:
  The results model is moved into its order without keeping track of what each move renumbered.

history:
  A ListModel moves one row at a time and every move renumbers the rows
  behind it, so an order made before the first move is wrong after it. The
  loop keeps a list of where each row stood; without it the rows land on
  the wrong places as soon as two of them change.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
          cur.splice(t, 0, cur.splice(j, 1)[0]);

replace:
          void 0;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_searchlogic.qml::test_an_order_lands_on_a_real_list_model.
  Line-neutral.
